From: steinmarder W11 cs-observer track
Subject: [PATCH 9/N] drm/radeon: wire ib_post_validate observer hook with
 absorbed packet_decode walk

Final observer hook (absorbs the originally-planned per-PKT3
packet_decode hook into a single post-validator IB walk).  Inserts
calls to radeon_palm_cs_observer_emit_ib_post_validate(&parser)
immediately before EVERY radeon_cs_parser_fini call in
radeon_cs_ioctl -- success path and error paths alike.  By that
point the chip-specific validator has run to completion regardless
of outcome, so the IB bytes the observer walks are exactly what
would have been (or would not have been) submitted to GPU.

The hook body walks parser->chunks[] for the IB chunk and:

  1. Decodes PM4 packet headers per R6xx/R7xx 3D Accel Guide.
  2. For each PKT3 packet whose opcode matches the
     SHADER_DESCRIPTOR_OPCODES allowlist (SET_CONFIG_REG,
     SET_CONTEXT_REG, SET_BOOL_CONST, SET_LOOP_CONST,
     SET_RESOURCE, SET_SAMPLER per Evergreen-Family ISA Ch.7),
     emits one packet_decode JSONL row with reg_addr_or_slot +
     payload_dwords (first 64).
  3. Computes crc32_le over the full IB and emits one
     ib_post_validate summary row with ib_length_dw +
     ib_crc32_le + total_packets + filtered_packets.

The summary row's ib_crc32_le can be compared against the
ib_chunk_pre_parse row's crc32_le (same chunk) by userspace to
detect kernel validator mutation -- the A1 != C discriminator in
the byte-path comparison decision table.

The merged single-callsite design avoids needing a second sed/awk
landmark inside evergreen_cs.c whose exact source layout varies
between r600_cs.c, evergreen_cs.c, ni.c, and si.c (each chip
family has its own cs_parse implementation).  The single landmark
in radeon_cs.c (radeon_cs_parser_fini) is chip-family-agnostic.

The prep-source.sh wiring inserts this hook once before every
radeon_cs_parser_fini callsite via one regex substitution.  That
produces one ib_post_validate event per error-path early return and
one per success-path out: fall-through.  No duplicate is emitted on
success because the success path reaches out: exactly once.

Assisted-by: Claude (Opus 4.7)
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/radeon/radeon_cs.c | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/radeon/radeon_cs.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/radeon/radeon_cs.c
@@ -380,6 +380,7 @@
 	r = radeon_cs_parser_relocs(&parser);
 	if (r) {
 		if (r != -ERESTARTSYS) DRM_ERROR("Failed to parse relocations !\n");
+		radeon_palm_cs_observer_emit_ib_post_validate(&parser);
 		radeon_cs_parser_fini(&parser, r, false);
 		mutex_unlock(&rdev->cs_mutex);
 		return r;
@@ -402,6 +403,7 @@
 out:
+	radeon_palm_cs_observer_emit_ib_post_validate(&parser);
 	radeon_cs_parser_fini(&parser, r, true);
 	mutex_unlock(&rdev->cs_mutex);
 	up_read(&rdev->exclusive_lock);
